#: queue/index.php:554 queue/intro.php:87
msgid "Add Domains Using an API"
msgstr "Add Domains Using an API"

#: queue/intro.php:53
msgid "The Domain Queue imports the details of your domains, such as their expiry dates and DNS servers, and adds them to your main %s database along with your domains. There are two ways to use it."
msgstr "The Domain Queue imports the details of your domains, such as their expiry dates and DNS servers, and adds them to your main %s database along with your domains. There are two ways to use it."

#: queue/intro.php:54
msgid "If %s supports your registrar's API, choose the registrar account and supply a list of domains, and the rest of the work is done for you. Depending on the registrar, you may not even have to supply the list of domains."
msgstr "If %s supports your registrar's API, choose the registrar account and supply a list of domains, and the rest of the work is done for you. Depending on the registrar, you may not even have to supply the list of domains."

#: queue/intro.php:55
msgid "If your registrar isn't supported, paste a list of your domains and their details are looked up using RDAP, the public replacement for WHOIS, or WHOIS itself for domains RDAP doesn't cover. WHOIS privacy and auto renewal are set to No, since neither one includes them."
msgstr "If your registrar isn't supported, paste a list of your domains and their details are looked up using RDAP, the public replacement for WHOIS, or WHOIS itself for domains RDAP doesn't cover. WHOIS privacy and auto renewal are set to No, since neither one includes them."

#: queue/intro.php:84
msgid "In order to use the Domain Queue you must set up the cron job that comes with %s."
msgstr "In order to use the Domain Queue you must set up the cron job that comes with %s."

#: queue/intro.php:85
msgid "For more information, please see the %sUser Guide%s."
msgstr "For more information, please see the %sUser Guide%s."

