msgstr "This script can only be run from the command line. To upgrade from your browser, sign in to %s as an administrator."

#: queue/add/rdap.php:155
msgid "Paste a list of domains and %s will look each one up using RDAP, the public replacement for WHOIS, or WHOIS itself for domains RDAP doesn't cover, filling in its expiry date and DNS servers and working out which registrar it's at, so you don't need to choose a registrar or enter any API details. A registrar that isn't in %s yet is added for you. Each domain goes into your account at that registrar if you have exactly one, or otherwise into a general account named \"RDAP Import\" that's created the first time and used for later imports."
msgstr "Paste a list of domains and %s will look each one up using RDAP, the public replacement for WHOIS, or WHOIS itself for domains RDAP doesn't cover, filling in its expiry date and DNS servers and working out which registrar it's at, so you don't need to choose a registrar or enter any API details. A registrar that isn't in %s yet is added for you. Each domain goes into your account at that registrar if you have exactly one, or otherwise into a general account named \"RDAP Import\" that's created the first time and used for later imports."

#: queue/add/rdap.php:158
msgid "Neither RDAP nor WHOIS includes a domain's WHOIS privacy or auto renewal status, so both will be set to No. You can update them afterwards using the Bulk Updater."
msgstr "Neither RDAP nor WHOIS includes a domain's WHOIS privacy or auto renewal status, so both will be set to No. You can update them afterwards using the Bulk Updater."

